### Payment Ledger Service (PSP) - REST API Routes
###
### Authentication
###   - /platform/* and /ledger/*: operator token (PLATFORM_ADMIN_TOKEN in .env)
###   - /v1/*: merchant secret key (sk_test_...), returned once by onboarding
### Idempotency (ADR 0004): every POST and DELETE requires Idempotency-Key.
###   Same key + same body replays the stored response (header Idempotent-Replayed: true);
###   same key + different body -> 422; request still running -> 409.
###   Keys are scoped per caller and remembered for 24 hours.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3001
@platformToken = dev-platform-token-troque-em-producao
# paste the values returned by "Onboard a merchant"
@merchantId = mch_replace_me
@secretKey = sk_test_replace_me
@apiKeyId = key_replace_me
@paymentId = pay_replace_me
@txid = replace_with_pix_txid
@webhookEndpointId = we_replace_me
@publishableKey = pk_test_replace_me
@cardToken = tok_replace_me
@refundId = re_replace_me
@payoutId = po_replace_me
@eventId = evt_replace_me

### ============================ PLATFORM ============================

### 1. POST - Onboard a merchant
### Optional "pixFeeBps" and "cardFeeBps": MDRs in basis points (defaults 99 = 0.99%
### on Pix, 299 = 2.99% on credit card).
### Creates the merchant, its ledger accounts (merchant:<id>:pending and
### merchant:<id>:available, BRL) and a secret + publishable key, atomically.
### Returns: 201 with the keys in plaintext. This is the only time they are shown:
### an idempotent replay returns them masked.
POST {{baseUrl}}/platform/merchants
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: onboard-loja-prateleira-1

{
  "name": "Loja Prateleira"
}

### 2. GET - Get a merchant
### Errors: 404 merchants.not_found
GET {{baseUrl}}/platform/merchants/{{merchantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}

### 2b. GET - Reconciliation report
### Cross-checks ledger, payments, refunds, payouts and the receivables schedule.
### Returns: { ok, checks: [{ name, ok, discrepancies }] }; a job runs it every
### RECONCILIATION_INTERVAL_MS and logs failed checks.
GET {{baseUrl}}/platform/reconciliation
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}

### 2c. GET - Pix in suspense (received, but matching no payable charge)
### status: open | returning | returned | return_failed
GET {{baseUrl}}/platform/suspense
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}

### 2d. POST - Return a Pix in suspense to its payer (devolução)
### Errors: 404 suspense.not_found | 422 suspense.already_handled
POST {{baseUrl}}/platform/suspense/E99999999202610211200abcdefghijk/return
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}
Idempotency-Key: suspense-return-1

### ============================= LEDGER =============================

### 3. POST - Post a manual adjustment to the ledger
### Operators only. Sources used by the PSP's own flows (pix, card, refund,
### payout, settlement, suspense-return) and merchant pending accounts are
### refused (422 ledger.reserved_source / ledger.pending_is_scheduled), so
### reconciliation can always explain where money came from.
### Rules:
###   - Amounts are integers in cents; positive = debit, negative = credit
###   - At least two entries, none zero, all in the same currency, summing to 0
###   - Every account must exist and hold the entry's currency
###   - (source, externalReference) is unique: posting it again returns the existing
###     transaction; posting it with different content -> 409
### Returns: 201 Created with the transaction
### Errors: 400 invalid body | 401 | 409 reference conflict | 422 business rule violated
POST {{baseUrl}}/ledger/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: 6f1c2a9e-0d4b-4c39-9a57-1f0e8a3b2c10

{
  "description": "Goodwill credit for a delayed payout",
  "source": "manual",
  "externalReference": "ticket-1234",
  "entries": [
    {
      "accountId": "rail-costs",
      "amount": 500,
      "currency": "BRL"
    },
    {
      "accountId": "merchant:{{merchantId}}:available",
      "amount": -500,
      "currency": "BRL"
    }
  ]
}

### 4. GET - List all ledger transactions
### Returns: Array of transactions with their entries, oldest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/ledger/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}

### 5. GET - List accounts with their balances
### Returns: Array of { id, type, currency, balance }; balance is the debit-positive
### sum of the account's entries, derived on every call. All balances sum to 0.
GET {{baseUrl}}/ledger/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}

### ======================= MERCHANT API (/v1) =======================

### 6. GET - The authenticated merchant
### Errors: 401 missing/invalid/revoked key | 403 publishable key
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/account
Authorization: Bearer {{secretKey}}

### 7. GET - Balance owed to the merchant
### Returns: { available: [{ amount, currency }], pending: [{ amount, currency }] },
### amounts in cents, derived from the ledger.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/balance
Authorization: Bearer {{secretKey}}

### 8. GET - List API keys (masked: "sk_test_…a1b2")
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/api_keys
Authorization: Bearer {{secretKey}}

### 9. POST - Create an API key ("secret" or "publishable")
### Returns: 201 with the key in plaintext, shown only this once.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/api_keys
Authorization: Bearer {{secretKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: create-key-1

{
  "type": "secret"
}

### 10. DELETE - Revoke an API key
### Idempotent: revoking a revoked key returns it unchanged.
### Errors: 404 merchants.api_key_not_found | 422 merchants.last_secret_key
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/v1/api_keys/{{apiKeyId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{secretKey}}
Idempotency-Key: revoke-key-1

### ============================ PAYMENTS ============================

### 11. POST - Create a Pix payment
### amount in cents (1 to 1_000_000_000); currency "BRL"; method "pix".
### Optional: description (<= 255), metadata (<= 20 string values),
### expiresInSeconds (60 to 86400, default 3600).
### Returns: 201 with status "pending", the fee and net amount, and
### pix.copiaECola (BR Code) for the payer. Emits payment.pending.
### Errors: 400 invalid body | 422 payments.unsupported_currency, payments.invalid_metadata
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{secretKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: cart-42-attempt-1

{
  "amount": 12345,
  "currency": "BRL",
  "method": "pix",
  "description": "Pedido 42",
  "metadata": { "cartId": "42" }
}

### 12. GET - List payments, newest first (?limit=1..100, default 20)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/payments?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{secretKey}}

### 13. GET - Get a payment
### Errors: 404 payments.not_found
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/payments/{{paymentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{secretKey}}

### 14. POST - Cancel a pending payment (or an uncaptured card authorization)
### Idempotent: canceling a canceled payment returns it unchanged. A card
### authorization is voided at the acquirer. Emits payment.canceled.
### Errors: 404 payments.not_found | 422 payments.not_cancelable
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/payments/{{paymentId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{secretKey}}
Idempotency-Key: cancel-1

### ============================== CARDS ==============================
### Test cards (simulated acquirer, ADR 0001):
###   4242 4242 4242 4242 approved (Visa)   5555 5555 5555 4444 approved (Mastercard)
###   4000 0000 0000 0002 card_declined     4000 0000 0000 9995 insufficient_funds
###   4000 0000 0000 0069 expired_card      4000 0000 0000 0119 processing_error
### Any future expiry and any 3-digit CVC (4 digits for Amex).

### 21. POST - Tokenize a card (from the payer's browser)
### Uses the PUBLISHABLE key. No Idempotency-Key on purpose (ADR 0005).
### Returns: 201 { id: "tok_...", card: { brand, last4, expMonth, expYear }, expiresAt }.
### The token is single use and valid for 15 minutes.
### Errors: 400 malformed | 422 vault.invalid_number, vault.expired_card,
###   vault.invalid_cvc, vault.unsupported_brand
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tokens
Authorization: Bearer {{publishableKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "card": {
    "number": "4242 4242 4242 4242",
    "expMonth": 12,
    "expYear": 2030,
    "cvc": "123",
    "holderName": "Marcos Teixeira"
  }
}

### 22. POST - Pay with a card
### Authorizes and captures before answering. "capture": false only authorizes
### (status "authorized"; capture within 7 days). "installments": 1 to 12.
### Returns: 201 with status "succeeded", "authorized", "failed" (with
### failure.code: card_declined, insufficient_funds, expired_card,
### processing_error) or, if the acquirer did not answer, "pending" (the
### outcome follows by webhook).
### Errors: 404 vault.token_not_found | 409 vault.token_used |
###   422 vault.token_expired, payments.card_mismatch
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{secretKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: cart-42-attempt-2

{
  "amount": 12345,
  "currency": "BRL",
  "method": "credit_card",
  "card": { "token": "{{cardToken}}", "installments": 3 },
  "metadata": { "cartId": "42" }
}

### 23. POST - Capture an authorized card payment
### Idempotent. Moves the money in the ledger. Emits payment.succeeded.
### Errors: 404 payments.not_found | 422 payments.not_capturable
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/payments/{{paymentId}}/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{secretKey}}
Idempotency-Key: capture-1

### ===================== REFUNDS, RECEIVABLES, PAYOUTS =====================
### ADR 0006. Outgoing money is recorded before the rail is called and
### compensated (never deleted) if the rail refuses.

### 24. POST - Refund a payment (all or part)
### The PSP keeps its fee: the merchant returns the full amount, first from the
### payment's unreleased receivables, then from the available balance (which
### may go negative). Full refund → payment status "refunded".
### Returns: 201 with status "succeeded", "failed" (failureCode) or "pending"
### (the rail did not answer; the outcome follows by webhook).
### Errors: 404 payments.not_found | 422 refunds.payment_not_refundable,
###   refunds.amount_not_refundable
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/refunds
Authorization: Bearer {{secretKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: refund-order-42

{
  "payment": "{{paymentId}}",
  "amount": 5000,
  "reason": "Cliente desistiu de um item"
}

### 25. GET - List refunds, newest first (?payment=pay_...&limit=1..100)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/refunds?payment={{paymentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{secretKey}}

### 26. GET - Get a refund
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/refunds/{{refundId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{secretKey}}

### 27. GET - Receivables schedule ("agenda de recebíveis"), soonest first
### ?released=false: still to come; ?released=true: already available.
### Pix: D+0. Card: D+30 per installment.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/receivables?released=false
Authorization: Bearer {{secretKey}}

### 28. PATCH - Set the payout Pix key
### CPF, CNPJ (check digits validated), e-mail, +55 phone or random key (EVP).
### In the simulator, "naoexiste@pix.example" makes payouts fail.
### Errors: 422 settlement.invalid_pix_key
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/v1/account
Authorization: Bearer {{secretKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: payout-key-1

{
  "payoutPixKey": "529.982.247-25"
}

### 29. POST - Pay out the available balance by Pix
### "amount" in cents (optional: defaults to everything available; minimum 100).
### Returns: 201 with status "paid", "failed" (failureCode, money back to the
### balance) or "pending".
### Errors: 422 settlement.no_payout_key, settlement.insufficient_balance,
###   settlement.amount_too_small
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/payouts
Authorization: Bearer {{secretKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: payout-2026-10-21

{}

### 30. GET - List payouts, newest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/payouts
Authorization: Bearer {{secretKey}}

### 31. GET - Get a payout
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/payouts/{{payoutId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{secretKey}}

### ============================ WEBHOOKS ============================
### Deliveries: POST <url> with the event as JSON and the header
###   PSP-Signature: t=<unix seconds>,v1=<hex HMAC-SHA256(secret, "<t>.<raw body>")>
### Retried with backoff (30s, 2m, 10m, 30m, 1h, 3h, 6h, 12h) until a 2xx answer.
### Deduplicate on the event id: delivery is at least once.

### 15. POST - Register a webhook endpoint
### Returns: 201 with the signing secret (whsec_...) in full, only this once.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/webhook_endpoints
Authorization: Bearer {{secretKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: webhook-endpoint-1

{
  "url": "http://localhost:3000/webhooks/payments"
}

### 16. GET - List webhook endpoints (secrets masked)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/webhook_endpoints
Authorization: Bearer {{secretKey}}

### 17. DELETE - Disable a webhook endpoint
### Idempotent. Pending deliveries to it are no longer sent.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/v1/webhook_endpoints/{{webhookEndpointId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{secretKey}}
Idempotency-Key: disable-endpoint-1

### 18. GET - List events, newest first (?type=payment.succeeded&limit=1..100)
### For reconciling what a webhook endpoint may have missed.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/events?type=payment.succeeded&limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{secretKey}}

### 19. GET - Get an event
### Errors: 404 webhooks.event_not_found
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/events/{{eventId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{secretKey}}

### =================== SIMULATOR (SIMULATORS_ENABLED) ===================
### Plays the payer and their bank (ADR 0001). No authentication; never
### enabled in production.

### 20. POST - Pay a Pix charge
### Optional "amount" (cents) to simulate a wrong amount: the money lands in the
### suspense account and the payment stays pending.
### Returns: 200 { endToEndId, outcome: "succeeded" | "unmatched" }
### Errors: 404 simulator.charge_not_found | 422 simulator.charge_not_payable
POST {{baseUrl}}/simulator/pix/{{txid}}/pay
Content-Type: application/json

{}
